WEBVTT

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:17.610
Maiden of purest white, answer:

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.230
Which wilt thou choose?
Blue water? Or storm clouds?

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:45.890
Fena! Let's go!

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:47.740
Oh. Sure.

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:29.030
You're <i>absolutely</i> sure
that this is the destination?

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:32.390
Absolutely positive!
Debar-Dodopepapin!

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:34.150
It's at Dendeden!

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:35.810
Wasn't it Deededeen?

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:38.140
Not even close!
It's Dendendekeden!

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:39.790
Oops, you're right!

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.660
Fine, that's enough.
I'll ask Fena later.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:45.800
Huh? Why?

00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:49.300
Libar-Oberstein.

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:51.800
They must mean Dresden.

00:02:52.010 --> 00:02:54.450
I knew it, those two
were way off base.

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:56.380
Roger that. Thanks.

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:00.440
Okay, that should do it.

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:03.900
I'll change it again tomorrow.

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:09.700
Oh, hey!

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:13.920
I'm sorry.
For acting on my own.

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:17.780
There's no need to keep apologizing.
You made your point the first time.

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:19.330
But I feel--

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:23.090
Our job is to protect you.
Don't worry about it.

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:28.720
I guess, but still... I'll work hard to be
at least a little useful to you guys.

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:31.140
Thank you, but that
won't be necessary.

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:34.990
For one thing, you're badly mistaken
if you think you can be helpful.

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:38.120
So stop putting yourself at risk.
Never do it again!

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:41.310
Like hell I will! I want to be useful
to you guys someday!

00:03:41.710 --> 00:03:44.330
That attitude is exactly what
makes trouble for us!

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:46.570
Pick fleas off your dog or something
to stay out of the way, idiot!

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:47.820
Never!

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:51.320
"Now, now..."

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:01.310
What is it?

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:04.090
It's not like you to raise
your voice like that.

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:08.090
Normally, you just whack people
 on the head.

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:12.340
Let me through.

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:40.840
Fena.

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:44.380
Shitan?

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:51.030
Your voices carried
through the whole ship.

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:56.640
Don't let Yukimaru get to you.
He's always like that.

00:05:00.010 --> 00:05:01.520
Say, Shitan...

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:04.270
Teach me how to use a weapon.

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:17.340
Why isn't it going very far?!

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:19.460
This is going to take a while...

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:22.370
I just had a thought.

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:26.420
Absolutely not!

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:29.850
Can't you help me out?
You and I are friends, right?

00:05:29.950 --> 00:05:32.610
I don't recall us
being <i>that</i> close.

00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:34.240
Besides!

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:38.140
I don't like that jerk's snooty implication
that "Oh, if Fena can't handle a bow,

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:40.180
surely a gun would be
easy enough for her!"

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:42.940
He knows when to beat
a hasty retreat.

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:47.890
And anyway, Fena, guns aren't something
you can master in a day!

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:51.420
First you have to study their construction,
tools, gunpowder, features, and history!

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:53.700
Only then can you start
actually training with them!

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:57.000
Actually, I want you to take a look
at this thing I just invented.

00:05:57.100 --> 00:06:01.200
It's based on the same principle as a bean
planting machine, using spin and gravity to--

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:05.060
Huh? Fena?
Where did you go? Fena?

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:05.060
Shitan...

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:07.580
That was just for laughs.
For fun.

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:10.590
GALLEY

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:15.700
Tsubaki! Got a minute?

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:21.400
Swordplay? You want <i>me</i>
to teach it?

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:23.350
To <i>you?</i> What for?

00:06:23.910 --> 00:06:27.010
Shitan said that since you're the person on
the ship who's closest to my skill level,

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:29.360
maybe I'd have an easier time
learning from you.

00:06:29.890 --> 00:06:31.690
Oh, that makes sense!

00:06:31.790 --> 00:06:35.950
So, long story short... Of everyone on
the ship, I'm the worst swordsman,

00:06:36.050 --> 00:06:38.320
so I'm the ideal person to teach
a total newbie like you.

00:06:38.420 --> 00:06:41.320
Sure, I get it...
That's what he's saying.

00:06:41.820 --> 00:06:42.870
SHITAN!

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:48.990
Tsubaki, is this that <i>sumashijiru</i> stuff?
It's so bland and simple.

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:51.750
Can I try dropping the head of a bonito
in here or something?

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:53.740
GET OUT!

00:06:56.670 --> 00:06:58.140
No way!

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:04.420
In the end, everybody
turned me down...

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:07.770
Am I really that hopeless?

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:17.260
I'll teach you. Swords aren't exactly
my strong suit, though.

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:21.640
Really? I always thought you were the sort
of person who was good at everything.

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:26.800
Hardly. I'd say I'm probably the worst
out of everyone on this ship.

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:28.490
Oh, no way!

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:32.540
No, it's the truth.
And actually,

00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:37.210
it's all because I was always around
someone who made me feel like

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:39.820
I'd never measure up
no matter how hard I tried.

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:47.140
I didn't want to be shown up by the guy,
so I always ran out ahead of him.

00:07:47.640 --> 00:07:51.440
But as a result, he had to save
my life again and again.

00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:55.360
So I thought, I want to
save <i>his</i> life next time.

00:07:55.770 --> 00:07:58.600
But not by running out ahead.
From behind.

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:04.140
So you took up the bow.

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:06.440
Let's head in.
It's getting cold.

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:10.330
Shitan!

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:18.840
I want to become strong enough to protect him
for a change, even if just a little.

00:08:18.940 --> 00:08:20.340
Just like you do!

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:26.400
We'll begin tomorrow.
Before breakfast.

00:08:42.550 --> 00:08:44.870
<i>I want to be able
to protect him...</i>

00:08:51.350 --> 00:08:53.150
Have you seen Shitan?

00:08:53.250 --> 00:08:54.860
Wha--? Shitan?

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:58.030
He's the only one who has
the screws for this barrel.

00:08:58.130 --> 00:09:00.780
- Look, um...
- About this morning...

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:04.020
Shitan was up on deck until just now!
Together with me!

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:05.690
I think he might have
gone back to his cabin!

00:09:05.790 --> 00:09:10.030
You know, I think I get the source of his
sex appeal! He's so relaxed around women!

00:09:10.130 --> 00:09:13.110
Him being handsome <i>and</i> a nice guy <i>and</i>
tough almost seems unfair, you know?

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:16.940
N-Not that I noticed!
Well, good night!

00:09:21.770 --> 00:09:23.270
Relaxed around women...

00:09:40.540 --> 00:09:41.140
Ow!

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:42.680
Again!

00:09:52.470 --> 00:09:55.940
One... One more time!

00:09:57.640 --> 00:10:01.590
Okay, Fena. Here's the one thing I can
teach you as the worst swordsman here.

00:10:01.690 --> 00:10:03.350
Draw it, and kill the other guy.

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:05.450
- Draw it, and kill the other guy.
- Yep!

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:24.590
You're late!

00:10:25.170 --> 00:10:26.890
All wrong! Elbows in!

00:10:26.990 --> 00:10:29.350
Your right elbow
is drooping!

00:10:29.640 --> 00:10:31.410
Your back's all wrong, too!

00:10:31.510 --> 00:10:33.350
Your elbows again!
Elbows!

00:10:33.760 --> 00:10:36.600
You want your elbow up like--

00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:41.510
If you shoot without my say-so again,
that's the last time you're touching it!

00:10:41.610 --> 00:10:42.640
- Is that clear?!
- Yes, ma'am.

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:44.680
- I can't hear you!
- Yes, ma'am!

00:10:44.780 --> 00:10:47.050
When you don't answer with gusto,
the gun doesn't respect you!

00:10:47.150 --> 00:10:49.120
You're a lousy shot because
the gun doesn't respect you!

00:10:54.280 --> 00:10:58.450
She takes so long... She takes forever
to read me the riot act...

00:11:02.130 --> 00:11:06.130
"Eat all of these."

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:49.190
Any little detail would help.
Can you tell us anything?

00:11:49.940 --> 00:11:53.280
The grinding definitely looks like
the method we use in this village,

00:11:53.380 --> 00:11:55.370
but we don't make anything
in this shape.

00:11:55.470 --> 00:11:57.240
Not anymore, at least.

00:11:57.340 --> 00:11:59.140
I don't believe it...

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:01.040
I'm sorry I couldn't be
of more help.

00:12:01.140 --> 00:12:02.830
Hold on.

00:12:19.160 --> 00:12:21.880
- Mind if I take a quick look?
- Arya, it isn't one of ours.

00:12:21.980 --> 00:12:24.100
- May I?
- Um, sure.

00:12:36.280 --> 00:12:37.490
Well, well.

00:12:38.970 --> 00:12:40.280
Where'd you get it?

00:12:40.390 --> 00:12:41.640
Er...

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:43.870
It's been passed down for generations
among my people.

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:47.010
Circumstances now dictate
that we learn more about it.

00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:50.610
We'd like to learn everything
we can, no matter how trivial.

00:12:50.710 --> 00:12:52.860
We'll repay you
as best we can.

00:12:54.510 --> 00:12:55.620
Ah.

00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:09.640
I'm Arya.
Nice to meet you.

00:13:10.340 --> 00:13:11.830
I'm Yukimaru.

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:14.740
- Nice to meet you, young lady.
- I-I'm Fena.

00:13:15.610 --> 00:13:19.780
For starters, I'll take you to someone
who probably knows about your stone.

00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:21.750
It's a bit of a hike, though.

00:13:22.540 --> 00:13:24.500
Thank you so much!

00:13:25.770 --> 00:13:29.500
All goods shipped from this village are
submitted to the Burgermeister for inspection.

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:33.510
For generations, we've been forbidden
from taking on jobs as individuals.

00:13:34.210 --> 00:13:36.940
- You don't inscribe them?
- It's our way.

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:40.010
- That's odd.
- I know, right?

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:44.520
Those who don't like it
pack up and leave.

00:13:46.040 --> 00:13:48.780
Yukimaru's talking to a woman
like it's no big deal...

00:13:48.880 --> 00:13:50.520
With a sexy one.

00:13:51.150 --> 00:13:53.890
- Is that sword of yours sharp?
- Sharp enough.

00:13:53.990 --> 00:13:56.430
- Who honed it?
- I did.

00:13:56.830 --> 00:13:58.260
You trained in it?

00:13:58.360 --> 00:13:59.990
- Physical contact!
- Oh, my...

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:03.120
I wouldn't say that. I just picked it up
as I went along.

00:14:03.220 --> 00:14:05.370
That's the best way to learn,
young man!

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:08.390
The adult two-step touch!

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:10.750
Her hand's gradually
moving inwards!

00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:13.380
Come on, ants, you're reading
too much into it.

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:16.220
They haven't seen many
women like her before.

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:18.880
It's just past that turn.

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:23.970
Okay, we're here.

00:14:32.280 --> 00:14:34.610
This is where the Burgermeister
does his work.

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:40.370
Wait here a minute.
He can be a little difficult.

00:14:43.990 --> 00:14:46.140
- What'll you do?
- About what?

00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:49.670
She's into you, friend. If you tried,
you could go all the way with her.

00:14:49.770 --> 00:14:51.770
Huh? Go where?

00:14:53.550 --> 00:14:56.630
It's okay! He says that
he'll let four of you come in.

00:14:57.030 --> 00:14:59.640
Yukimaru! I have a favor to ask,
if you don't mind.

00:15:49.140 --> 00:15:53.600
If we stay the night here, that woman
is going to sneak into Yukimaru's bed.

00:15:53.890 --> 00:15:55.890
H-How can you be so sure?

00:15:55.990 --> 00:15:58.070
Many years of experience.

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:00.850
Is this all right?

00:16:01.380 --> 00:16:04.100
Thank you!
Grandpa, he's finished!

00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:12.580
This is amazing work.

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:16.090
- You like it?
- Of course!

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:21.920
This knife was given to me by
my father when I was a little boy.

00:16:22.590 --> 00:16:25.100
I wanted it so badly.
I kept pestering him.

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:32.700
It gleamed and shone just like this.
This brings back memories.

00:16:35.060 --> 00:16:37.480
I must repay the favor.

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:48.190
- I'm bored...
- We haven't had scenes in a while.

00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:51.440
Makaba, I'd get a line in
if I were you.

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:53.750
This is delicious!

00:16:55.890 --> 00:16:57.250
Now then...

00:16:57.390 --> 00:17:00.630
You wish to know
about this stone, then?

00:17:01.190 --> 00:17:02.140
Yes.

00:17:02.240 --> 00:17:06.140
To make a long story short, this stone
was definitely made here in this village.

00:17:06.550 --> 00:17:09.640
- You mean it?!
- You were right, Fena!

00:17:10.370 --> 00:17:13.640
Do you know when it was made?
And where? And what it's for?

00:17:14.320 --> 00:17:17.140
When a product is being prepared
to be shipped out,

00:17:17.240 --> 00:17:20.320
we scratch it in a way that's
invisible to the naked eye.

00:17:20.420 --> 00:17:24.080
We use it to keep a record of its production
date and who commissioned it.

00:17:24.300 --> 00:17:28.670
This stone has "D3756"
etched into it.

00:17:29.380 --> 00:17:31.290
- Arya.
- Yes?

00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:35.670
Go fetch me the blue book
from that shelf.

00:17:55.790 --> 00:17:58.190
This is most unusual.

00:17:58.890 --> 00:18:04.250
The stone itself didn't originate
from here. The client brought it?

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:10.200
From France. Year of production, 1436.
The client's name was...

00:18:11.640 --> 00:18:14.470
What on earth?
Is this some sort of joke?

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:16.400
Hm? What's it say?

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:18.080
What's the matter?

00:18:22.260 --> 00:18:26.090
Client, La Pucelle d'Orléans.

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:29.590
La Pucelle d'Orléans?

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:31.600
Hang on, does this mean...

00:18:32.680 --> 00:18:36.100
Does this mean it was commissioned
by Joan of Arc?

00:18:37.390 --> 00:18:40.440
Look here at the signature. It's hard
to make out, but that says "Jeanne."

00:18:40.540 --> 00:18:43.040
Really? If that's true,
that's amazing, right?

00:18:43.140 --> 00:18:45.050
It does seem to be a joke.

00:18:45.150 --> 00:18:47.110
That is of no concern.

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:51.370
The order being from Joan of Arc is no
big deal? Is that what you're saying?

00:18:52.280 --> 00:18:55.840
A client being famous
is of no concern to us.

00:18:56.240 --> 00:18:59.390
We count da Vinci and Columbus
among our clients.

00:18:59.530 --> 00:19:02.380
We've even had many an order
from royal families around the world.

00:19:02.760 --> 00:19:05.280
What is it, then?

00:19:05.380 --> 00:19:08.380
The problem is that it
lists the year as 1436.

00:19:08.930 --> 00:19:12.820
1436...

00:19:13.980 --> 00:19:17.140
Joan of Arc was burned at the stake
in Rouen's market square--

00:19:18.100 --> 00:19:22.400
In 1431.

00:19:26.140 --> 00:19:31.410
This says that this stone was made
five years after Joan of Arc's execution.

00:19:32.570 --> 00:19:35.860
Commissioned by Joan of Arc herself.

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:50.350
Did that help a little?

00:19:50.450 --> 00:19:53.730
More than a little.
We'll never forget your kindness.

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:55.930
Arya, thank you so much!

00:19:56.650 --> 00:19:58.370
You're quite welcome.

00:19:58.930 --> 00:20:01.440
Say, why not stay the night
before you go?

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:07.290
I appreciate the offer,
but we must move swiftly.

00:20:07.390 --> 00:20:08.940
We must take our leave here.

00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:13.490
Oh, I see. I understand.
Be careful, wherever you're headed.

00:20:13.590 --> 00:20:15.450
I'll be praying for you
to have a safe journey.

00:20:22.210 --> 00:20:23.210
Fena!

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:27.460
Hang in there, okay?

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:52.490
You'll catch cold.

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:57.990
They sure were nice,
weren't they?

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:01.670
Yes. They were very
pleasant people.

00:21:03.690 --> 00:21:05.000
Yukimaru.

00:21:06.300 --> 00:21:08.500
I've... heard it before.

00:21:09.050 --> 00:21:12.130
You've heard it before?
Heard what?

00:21:14.270 --> 00:21:16.010
The word "la Pucelle."

00:21:18.910 --> 00:21:21.770
Like maybe I used to
call someone that.

00:21:22.260 --> 00:21:25.240
Or maybe someone
used to call <i>me</i> that.

00:21:40.360 --> 00:21:41.910
La Pucelle...

00:21:52.590 --> 00:21:53.670
What?

00:21:54.420 --> 00:21:56.300
I've been informed that
they've set out.
